                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239228885",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198063205732",
                            "num_reviews": 30,
                            "playtime_forever": 3332,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 980,
                            "playtime_at_review": 2904,
                            "last_played": 1794281621
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game has very intriguing mechanics and will give you engineering challenges you had not considered. The logic blocks work more like building a circuit board, and getting an elevator or airlock working will rack your brain. Every problem has multiple solutions; the simple solution and the working solution. \nFor example, a 3 story elevator. You can stack two pistons and put two switches that control them. You can control these switches manually like a simpleton, or you can use logic to make the elevator work like a real one. Most of the reviews that are negative are from players who were too STUPID to figure out how to make it work, too LAZY to take the time, too ENTITLED to realize their engineering problems were their own to fix and not the dev. \nI made my elevator work. It took almost a week and required me to reverse engineer it from someone else's design. Maybe you're smarter than me, and figure it out yourself. Maybe you're dumber than me, and can't do it at all. Either way, I want more content so make sure to buy this game so the dev keeps working on it.",
